.TH batten-mcp-grant 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-mcp\-grant \- Apply the committed MCP permissions to whichever server name the host exposed this session
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten mcp grant\fR [\fB\-\-guard\fR] [\fB\-\-aliases\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-settings\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fItool\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply the committed MCP permissions to whichever server name the host exposed this session
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-guard\fR
Read a hook payload on stdin and refuse the call the committed settings deny
.TP
\fB\-\-aliases\fR
List the portable alias each server in the injected config resolves to
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<config>\fR
The host\-injected MCP config to resolve server names through
.TP
\fB\-\-settings\fR \fI<settings>\fR
The permission settings file to judge, instead of the declared one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fItool\fR]
The tool name to resolve, as `mcp__<server>__<tool>`; absent under \-\-guard or \-\-aliases
